# Flutter/Dart build state. `.dart_tool/chrome-device/` is a full Chrome profile
# written by `flutter run -d chrome`; 227 of its files were committed, including
# ones named `Login Data`, `Network/Cookies` and a browser `History`. They were
# inspected and held no credentials, no cookies and no autofill -- only 11
# localhost URLs from local runs -- but the directory must not be tracked, or the
# next run will commit real browsing data.
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Downloaded sentence-transformer weights (~87 MB). Cached explicitly rather than
# left inside node_modules so CI can restore it between runs.
hr-backend/.model-cache/

# The model service is a separate package with its own dependency tree -- that
# separation is the point of it, so it has its own node_modules.
model-service/node_modules/
model-service/.model-cache/

# Notifications are written through to a file so a restart does not lose every
# decision anyone was told about. Runtime state, not source.
hr-backend/.data/
